Package: nfsroot-watchdog
Architecture: all
Depends: busybox-static, mount, util-linux, ${misc:Depends}
Description: reboot NFS-root clients whose root has changed underneath them
 A machine booted from an NFS root caches handles to the files it uses. When
 the server replaces those files (a package upgrade, a configuration run),
 the client gets "Stale file handle" for them until it reboots, while
 everything already running carries on as if nothing happened.
 .
 nfsroot-watchdog checks once a minute and reboots the machine when the
 server marks its root as updated (see nfsroot-watchdog-server), or when
 known files stay stale. It waits while an update is in progress, and staggers
 the reboots of a whole fleet so that no two machines go down together. It runs
 from a static busybox copied into /run at boot, so a stale root cannot stop
 it.
 .
 Install this in the client root. It does nothing on a machine whose root is
 not NFS.

Package: nfsroot-watchdog-server
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, ${misc:Depends}
Description: mark NFS-root updates as finished for nfsroot-watchdog clients
 nfsroot-generation takes an update lock inside an exported NFS root before
 it is changed, and afterwards bumps a generation marker if anything really
 changed, then releases the lock. nfsroot-watchdog clients hold still while
 the lock exists and reboot themselves, staggered, once the generation
 changes.
 .
 Install this on the machine that updates the root.
